{# Rendered by VisitorDetails::renderVisitorDetails() into the visits log entry for one visit.

   The values were HTML-encoded on the way in: the write path sanitises every tracking parameter
   before storing it, so what the table holds is already encoded. Printing it under
   Twig's autoescape would encode it a second time and show the entities on screen. `rawSafeDecoded`
   is the filter for that: it decodes once and re-encodes exactly once, and every core visits log
   template that prints a stored label uses it -- see plugins/CustomDimensions/templates/_visitorDetails.twig
   and plugins/Live/templates/_visitorDetails.twig.

   Note also what this template does *not* use: `visitorLogIconWithDetails`. That class is Live's
   icon-strip contract -- its JavaScript reads a nested list out of the element and shows it as a
   tooltip -- so borrowing it for a line of text produces an empty tooltip on hover. Plain text
   belongs in `visitorLogTooltip`, as CustomDimensions does. #}
<div class="exampleLogTablesAttributes">
    {% if plan %}
        <br/>
        <abbr class="visitorLogTooltip" title="{{ 'ExampleLogTables_StoredByThisPlugin'|translate }}">{{ 'ExampleLogTables_UserPlan'|translate }}:</abbr>
        {{ plan|truncate(30)|rawSafeDecoded }}
    {% endif %}
    {% if account %}
        <br/>
        <abbr class="visitorLogTooltip" title="{{ 'ExampleLogTables_StoredByThisPlugin'|translate }}">{{ 'ExampleLogTables_UserAccount'|translate }}:</abbr>
        {{ account|truncate(30)|rawSafeDecoded }}
    {% endif %}
</div>
